1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000


2
00:00:08,475 --> 00:00:10,510
JULY 27, 2:00 P.M.

3
00:00:35,402 --> 00:00:37,737
The lightning is getting closer, right?

4
00:00:37,804 --> 00:00:39,739
Let's find a safe place to wait this out.

5
00:00:39,806 --> 00:00:41,041
Yes!

6
00:00:42,675 --> 00:00:43,943
So cold.

7
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:50,850
I'll boil some water now, Mr. Nikaido.

8
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,689
Mr. Nikaido, keep your stance low.

9
00:00:56,756 --> 00:00:58,024
Crouch down!

10
00:00:58,091 --> 00:01:00,460
I can't get any reception.

11
00:01:00,527 --> 00:01:02,228
Well yeah, we're in the mountains.

12
00:01:02,295 --> 00:01:04,631
-They told you to sit…
-Shut up! You're always…

13
00:01:04,697 --> 00:01:05,698
So close!

14
00:01:05,765 --> 00:01:07,300
Too close! This is bad!

15
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:08,835
Crouch down low.

16
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:10,804
-Calm down.
-Remain calm.

17
00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:12,939
Calm down and don't move.

18
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:16,376
My fingers feel all prickly.

19
00:01:17,444 --> 00:01:18,645
Cover your ears!

20
00:01:31,958 --> 00:01:33,493
During disasters…

21
00:01:34,527 --> 00:01:38,198
After three days,
chances of survival drastically drop.

22
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:42,235
We refer to them as,
"The critical 72 hours"

23
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:44,871
and they are
an important guideline for rescuers.

24
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:48,208
Nono…

25
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:50,143
Nono…

26
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:51,744
Nono…

27
00:02:17,103 --> 00:02:18,104
Mr. Awashima?

28
00:02:18,171 --> 00:02:19,672
Did you get some sleep, Ogoma?

29
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:22,442
Was anyone found?

30
00:02:22,509 --> 00:02:25,245
No. All six of them are still missing.

31
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:28,214
At dawn,
the rescue team will enter the mountain.

32
00:02:28,748 --> 00:02:30,150
I have a bad feeling.

33
00:02:30,216 --> 00:02:32,519
-Could you come to the scene early?
-Got it.

34
00:02:36,256 --> 00:02:38,458
Okay, all set.

35
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:56,176
SHIKARA POLICE STATION

36
00:02:56,242 --> 00:02:58,444
Please be careful.

37
00:02:58,511 --> 00:02:59,979
On to the next news.

38
00:03:00,046 --> 00:03:02,615
At Mount Shikara
in Shikara Town, Hokkaido,

39
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:06,319
six hikers are still missing.

40
00:03:06,986 --> 00:03:10,423
They were scheduled to descend
the mountain yesterday afternoon.

41
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:12,292
However, contact was lost,

42
00:03:12,825 --> 00:03:16,162
and the tour company
reported to the police

43
00:03:16,229 --> 00:03:19,866
that five mountain tour participants
and one guide had not returned.

44
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:23,036
The police believe that the six
are lost in the mountain

45
00:03:23,102 --> 00:03:26,539
and plan to begin
search operations at dawn.

46
00:03:29,576 --> 00:03:34,280
Among the missing are…

47
00:04:10,717 --> 00:04:13,286
I will explain the search plan.

48
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:16,122
Search teams one to three
will search the eastern stream.

49
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:17,190
Yes!

50
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,626
Paramedic teams one and two
will search the southern ridge,

51
00:04:19,692 --> 00:04:23,863
the area near the summit and the forest,
and along the cliff…

52
00:04:28,401 --> 00:04:29,535
Mr. Awashima.

53
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:31,304
Memorize the document.

54
00:04:31,371 --> 00:04:32,305
Okay.

55
00:04:34,641 --> 00:04:36,843
Did you get in touch with their families?

56
00:04:36,909 --> 00:04:38,645
They are waiting at their homes.

57
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:42,515
Do we know what
the missing hikers were wearing?

58
00:04:42,582 --> 00:04:46,019
No, we also have no eyewitnesses.
The mountain doesn't have much to offer.

59
00:04:46,886 --> 00:04:49,589
They had a guide called
Ms. Tabatake with them, right?

60
00:04:49,656 --> 00:04:51,591
So they are not all experienced hikers.

61
00:04:51,658 --> 00:04:53,293
I have a bad feeling.

62
00:04:53,359 --> 00:04:55,862
It's only been half a day.

63
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:59,699
Last night in the mountains,
it dropped to eight degrees.

64
00:04:59,766 --> 00:05:02,368
I'll go over the names
of the six to be rescued.

65
00:05:02,435 --> 00:05:04,671
The guide, Ms. Motoka Tabatake.

66
00:05:04,737 --> 00:05:07,640
Mr. Ryutaro Monden, Mrs. Misaki Monden,
a married couple.

67
00:05:07,707 --> 00:05:09,442
-Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.
-Yes.

68
00:05:09,509 --> 00:05:11,077
-Ms. Aya Saruwatari.
-Yes.

69
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:12,578
-Mr. Hitoshi Uematsu.
-Yes.

70
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:14,747
-That is all.
-Aya Saruwatari…

71
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:16,149
AYA SARUWATARI (38)

72
00:05:16,215 --> 00:05:17,884
-Let's depart!
-Yes!

73
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:23,723
I hope they are all found safe.

74
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:27,026
Search operations are currently ongoing…

75
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:28,394
Are you feeling all right?

76
00:05:29,729 --> 00:05:30,997
Everything looks all right.

77
00:05:31,064 --> 00:05:32,598
Her condition is stable.

78
00:05:33,132 --> 00:05:35,501
Nono, did you eat breakfast?

79
00:05:35,568 --> 00:05:39,906
The tour company contacted the police,
reporting a missing guide.

80
00:05:39,972 --> 00:05:42,675
According to police, the six
are believed to have gotten lost,

81
00:05:42,742 --> 00:05:44,977
and their whereabouts remain unknown.

82
00:05:45,044 --> 00:05:46,079
Since yesterday afternoon…

83
00:05:46,145 --> 00:05:47,780
Good morning.

84
00:05:49,816 --> 00:05:51,784
Yes, this is Shikara Police Station.

85
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:55,188
Hello, this is Yoshino
from Doto General Hospital.

86
00:05:55,254 --> 00:05:58,658
I would like to inquire about
the mountain accident on Mount Shikara.

87
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:02,595
Ms. Nono Tabatake,
who is hospitalized at our hospital,

88
00:06:02,662 --> 00:06:07,333
is worried because she cannot get in touch
with her mother, Ms. Motoka Tabatake.

89
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,269
I'll transfer you to the corresponding
department. Please wait a moment.

90
00:06:17,076 --> 00:06:19,645
-Drone team to base.
-Base to drone team, go ahead.

91
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:23,783
Elevation 780 meters, off to the west side
from Mount Shikara's ridge trail.

92
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:28,354
On the southeastern slope below the cliff,
we spotted a person in white clothing.

93
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:29,355
Copy that.

94
00:06:31,491 --> 00:06:34,460
Paramedics to base. We have made contact.

95
00:06:34,527 --> 00:06:36,829
A male, believed to be in his 40s.

96
00:06:38,297 --> 00:06:40,166
Level 300, rigor mortis present.

97
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,834
Suffered trauma to the head.

98
00:06:42,335 --> 00:06:44,604
It's our turn. Let's go.

99
00:06:45,171 --> 00:06:46,005
Okay.

100
00:06:48,808 --> 00:06:52,011
HOKKAIDO POLICE

101
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:06,759
Your pace is too fast!

102
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:09,128
-Ogoma!
-This is nothing!

103
00:07:09,195 --> 00:07:10,396
Watch your step.

104
00:07:10,463 --> 00:07:11,297
Yes.

105
00:07:12,732 --> 00:07:14,200
Hey, don't run!

106
00:07:19,071 --> 00:07:20,640
Hey!

107
00:07:20,706 --> 00:07:22,275
Can you hear us?

108
00:07:22,341 --> 00:07:23,810
Mr. Nikaido?

109
00:07:23,876 --> 00:07:25,878
Ms. Saruwatari!

110
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:27,680
Is anyone there?

111
00:07:27,747 --> 00:07:29,749
Hey!

112
00:07:31,551 --> 00:07:32,919
He fell from over there?

113
00:07:32,985 --> 00:07:33,820
Yes.

114
00:07:33,886 --> 00:07:35,688
He was way off the mountain trail.

115
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:38,291
He probably couldn't see ahead
because of the branches and grass.

116
00:07:38,357 --> 00:07:40,159
-Any others?
-No, he's alone.

117
00:07:40,226 --> 00:07:42,261
Why did he get separated from the group?

118
00:07:42,328 --> 00:07:44,330
He was wearing
just a short-sleeved T-shirt.

119
00:07:44,397 --> 00:07:46,199
Rain gear… this isn't his own.

120
00:07:46,265 --> 00:07:48,734
Why was he acting alone,
dressed like this?

121
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:51,337
Why did a beginner stray from the guide?

122
00:07:51,404 --> 00:07:55,007
-Don't just ask questions. Think--
-I'm thinking as I talk.

123
00:07:55,074 --> 00:07:56,008
Go ahead.

124
00:07:57,844 --> 00:08:00,646
Did he hit his head as he fell?

125
00:08:19,932 --> 00:08:20,833
Hey.

126
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:23,803
I'm fine.

127
00:08:25,104 --> 00:08:26,772
What is the time of death?

128
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:29,809
We'll conduct a detailed autopsy
once we get down the mountain…

129
00:08:29,876 --> 00:08:31,143
Just a rough estimate.

130
00:08:31,777 --> 00:08:35,314
He likely passed away yesterday
between 3:00 p.m. and 6:00 p.m.

131
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:48,094
It got pretty cold
in the mountain yesterday.

132
00:08:48,661 --> 00:08:52,798
He might have developed hypothermia,
lost consciousness and fell.

133
00:08:55,801 --> 00:08:57,803
Let's request a post-mortem autopsy.

134
00:08:59,171 --> 00:09:00,873
I want some kind of clue.

135
00:09:01,407 --> 00:09:04,777
Search team six reporting back. We found
a driver's license among his belongings.

136
00:09:04,844 --> 00:09:06,913
The victim is believed to be
Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.

137
00:09:08,915 --> 00:09:10,182
Watch your steps.

138
00:09:11,984 --> 00:09:14,086
-Yes?
-This is the Shikara Police Station.

139
00:09:14,153 --> 00:09:15,121
The police?

140
00:09:15,187 --> 00:09:17,223
Are you Mrs. Harune Nikaido?

141
00:09:19,025 --> 00:09:19,859
Yes.

142
00:09:20,426 --> 00:09:22,295
We regret to inform you

143
00:09:22,361 --> 00:09:25,965
that your husband, Mr. Teruyuki,
passed away on Mount Shikara.

144
00:09:28,167 --> 00:09:29,502
He died?

145
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:31,604
LIFE INSURANCE

146
00:09:31,671 --> 00:09:34,106
-It's uneven here. Please be careful.
-Yes.

147
00:09:34,173 --> 00:09:37,710
HOKKAIDO POLICE

148
00:09:37,777 --> 00:09:38,811
Okay.

149
00:09:39,378 --> 00:09:41,380
48 HOURS LEFT

150
00:09:41,881 --> 00:09:45,117
Huh? His body was just found, wasn't it?

151
00:09:45,184 --> 00:09:46,118
Yes, and yet

152
00:09:46,185 --> 00:09:50,022
the insurance company already received
an inquiry about his life insurance.

153
00:09:50,823 --> 00:09:54,560
What a calm and composed wife.

154
00:09:54,627 --> 00:09:56,362
She is a strange one.

155
00:09:57,163 --> 00:09:58,397
How much is the payout?

156
00:09:58,464 --> 00:10:00,433
150 million yen.

157
00:10:00,499 --> 00:10:01,534
Oh wow.

158
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:04,270
The contract was originally
for 50 million yen,

159
00:10:04,337 --> 00:10:06,405
but they suddenly increased it
two months ago.

160
00:10:06,472 --> 00:10:08,174
Well, well.

161
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,308
I sent over the details.

162
00:10:09,375 --> 00:10:10,209
Read them to me.

163
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,477
Read them yourself.

164
00:10:11,544 --> 00:10:12,945
I'm driving right now.

165
00:10:15,214 --> 00:10:18,351
The insured is Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido,
44 years old.

166
00:10:18,417 --> 00:10:21,053
He ran a restaurant in Asahikawa.

167
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:23,956
The beneficiary is his wife,
Ms. Harune, 58 years old.

168
00:10:24,023 --> 00:10:25,858
A 14-year difference? Any children?

169
00:10:25,925 --> 00:10:26,859
No.

170
00:10:26,926 --> 00:10:29,695
Harune will receive it all by herself.

171
00:10:30,396 --> 00:10:32,965
An older wife
receiving 150 million yen, huh.

172
00:10:33,532 --> 00:10:35,434
I wonder what kind of person she is.

173
00:10:46,612 --> 00:10:48,481
Sounds fishy, huh. Are you listening?

174
00:10:48,547 --> 00:10:50,049
Yeah, I'm listening.

175
00:10:50,116 --> 00:10:52,418
It was a mountain accident,
but schedule an appointment…

176
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:53,619
Stop!

177
00:10:53,686 --> 00:10:54,353
Stop!

178
00:10:56,389 --> 00:10:57,757
The white minivan!

179
00:10:58,357 --> 00:10:59,792
Pull over to the left and stop!

180
00:10:59,859 --> 00:11:01,961
A red convertible
escaping towards Abashiri…

181
00:11:02,028 --> 00:11:04,730
-Get out of the car.
-The number plate is…

182
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:07,733
Driver's license and car registration.

183
00:11:08,734 --> 00:11:11,637
Speeding violation, two penalty points.

184
00:11:11,704 --> 00:11:13,305
And a fine of 15,000 yen.

185
00:11:13,372 --> 00:11:15,708
Oh, I didn't realize I was over the limit.

186
00:11:15,775 --> 00:11:17,643
Please pay within eight days.

187
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,912
-What about that red sports car?
-My colleagues will handle it.

188
00:11:19,979 --> 00:11:22,314
There's no one around!
Isn't this pointless?

189
00:11:22,381 --> 00:11:23,616
You still violated the law.

190
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:25,518
You have an enforcement quota, don't you?

191
00:11:25,584 --> 00:11:27,520
-Nao.
-I hate that part about you police.

192
00:11:27,586 --> 00:11:30,923
Only doing what
the higher-ups tell you to…

193
00:11:30,990 --> 00:11:33,292
-Nao! That's not the way to go!
-Here you go.

194
00:11:33,359 --> 00:11:34,760
What?

195
00:11:34,827 --> 00:11:36,662
Nao, don't pick a fight with them.

196
00:11:36,729 --> 00:11:39,598
In this job, we often rely
on the police, you know.

197
00:11:39,665 --> 00:11:42,968
Don't you think it's them
who have to rely on us,

198
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,236
more often than not?

199
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:46,305
Well, that's true too, but…

200
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:49,508
Nao, smile.

201
00:11:54,814 --> 00:11:55,881
Hello.

202
00:12:06,759 --> 00:12:07,860
It's my husband…

203
00:12:38,157 --> 00:12:40,392
Must be tough for her, huh?

204
00:12:41,293 --> 00:12:44,964
Well, yeah. Her husband
was fine until yesterday…

205
00:12:53,672 --> 00:12:54,874
What's wrong?

206
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:57,276
She felt unwell.

207
00:12:57,343 --> 00:12:58,611
Would you like to sit down?

208
00:12:58,677 --> 00:12:59,812
Bathroom.

209
00:13:01,046 --> 00:13:02,314
Ms. Nikaido.

210
00:13:02,848 --> 00:13:04,717
How are you feeling?

211
00:13:06,018 --> 00:13:07,419
I'm fine.

212
00:13:38,384 --> 00:13:39,218
MISSING PERSONS LIST

213
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:42,855
If we don't find them today, we check
the north side tomorrow, I suppose.

214
00:13:42,922 --> 00:13:43,823
Yeah.

215
00:13:43,889 --> 00:13:47,126
Hello. Where is Ms. Harune Nikaido?

216
00:13:47,193 --> 00:13:48,360
Who might you be?

217
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:51,964
Excuse me.

218
00:13:52,464 --> 00:13:53,699
She's busy right now.

219
00:13:53,766 --> 00:13:56,135
-Who are you?
-Could you let me talk to her?

220
00:13:56,202 --> 00:13:57,236
Do it another day.

221
00:13:57,303 --> 00:13:59,104
Oh, my. I can't…

222
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:01,240
We are way past our scheduled time.

223
00:14:01,307 --> 00:14:03,175
Ms. Nikaido, are you okay?

224
00:14:03,242 --> 00:14:04,977
Sorry for making you wait.

225
00:14:05,044 --> 00:14:07,446
You have my condolences.

226
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:13,552
INVESTIGATOR - TSUKASA NAO

227
00:14:13,619 --> 00:14:14,453
"Choku…"

228
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,589
It's Nao. Tsukasa Nao.

229
00:14:16,655 --> 00:14:18,290
I'm an insurance investigator.

230
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:21,260
I need to ask a few questions
about the late Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido's

231
00:14:21,327 --> 00:14:23,262
life insurance.

232
00:14:23,829 --> 00:14:25,431
An insurance investigator is here.

233
00:14:25,497 --> 00:14:26,899
Oh, for what?

234
00:14:26,966 --> 00:14:29,335
Something about life insurance.

235
00:14:29,401 --> 00:14:31,670
The body was only just found!

236
00:14:31,737 --> 00:14:33,706
Who is this guy?

237
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:39,078
He's from Zennichi Insurance Research.
Tsukasa Nao.

238
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:41,046
Tsukasa Nao?

239
00:14:41,113 --> 00:14:43,082
He always acts so fast.

240
00:14:46,418 --> 00:14:47,887
Two months ago,

241
00:14:49,088 --> 00:14:52,725
the insurance contract was changed.

242
00:14:53,259 --> 00:14:55,261
Do you know why?

243
00:14:56,662 --> 00:14:57,596
I don't know.

244
00:14:58,931 --> 00:15:01,133
Did your husband often go
mountain climbing?

245
00:15:01,634 --> 00:15:06,238
Yesterday, I thought he was
playing golf with friends.

246
00:15:06,305 --> 00:15:10,175
So you don't usually know his plans?

247
00:15:10,776 --> 00:15:11,677
No.

248
00:15:12,378 --> 00:15:16,582
Why do you think he went to the mountains?

249
00:15:20,552 --> 00:15:21,820
You don't know?

250
00:15:22,955 --> 00:15:24,323
Were you two on good terms?

251
00:15:25,791 --> 00:15:26,692
We were normal.

252
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:30,429
When did you last eat with Mr. Teruyuki?

253
00:15:30,496 --> 00:15:34,066
Dinner? Lunch? Breakfast?

254
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:36,602
Can't you remember?

255
00:15:38,137 --> 00:15:40,039
-It's too sudden. She can't…
-Hey, you.

256
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:43,776
Let me change the question.
Were you satisfied with your husband?

257
00:15:44,476 --> 00:15:48,881
Be it money-wise, emotionally,
sexually… anything.

258
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:50,950
-Hey.
-You can choose not to answer.

259
00:15:51,016 --> 00:15:54,186
-Could you be quiet for a moment?
-Did you have an appointment with him?

260
00:15:54,253 --> 00:15:55,821
What time was your appointment?

261
00:15:58,123 --> 00:16:00,292
I've never met him before.

262
00:16:00,359 --> 00:16:02,528
An appointment? Did I say I had one?

263
00:16:02,594 --> 00:16:04,663
-Please come with me.
-Hey, what…

264
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:06,332
-What?
-Sorry.

265
00:16:06,398 --> 00:16:08,233
We are doing a police investigation here.

266
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,636
I see. I got scolded by the police again.

267
00:16:10,703 --> 00:16:12,338
Why don't you choose your words better?

268
00:16:12,404 --> 00:16:14,907
You can't say that to someone
who just lost family.

269
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:15,975
What's wrong with it?

270
00:16:16,041 --> 00:16:18,477
I don't like how
you pressured her so suddenly.

271
00:16:18,544 --> 00:16:20,412
I'm not working to impress you.

272
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:22,381
-Passing through.
-She's grieving!

273
00:16:22,448 --> 00:16:25,250
This is my job.
In insurance, speed is everything.

274
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:28,120
I'm racing against time too.

275
00:16:28,187 --> 00:16:30,889
I have five missing people.
I want to get any clue I can.

276
00:16:30,956 --> 00:16:31,790
But…

277
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:34,326
the family's feelings come first, got it?

278
00:16:34,393 --> 00:16:35,361
Are you…

279
00:16:35,961 --> 00:16:37,763
really a police officer?

280
00:16:38,364 --> 00:16:41,900
Don't the police
think everyone is a thief?

281
00:16:41,967 --> 00:16:43,736
I've never thought that way.

282
00:16:43,802 --> 00:16:46,972
Are you a foolishly good man?
Or a weakling who wants to look good?

283
00:16:47,039 --> 00:16:47,873
Which are you?

284
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:49,108
What did you say?

285
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:50,909
Too rough.

286
00:16:54,213 --> 00:16:55,347
Yes, what is it?

287
00:16:55,414 --> 00:16:57,182
-Found a hiker!
-A missing hiker has been found.

288
00:16:58,350 --> 00:16:59,551
Who?

289
00:16:59,618 --> 00:17:02,321
Search team to headquarters.
We found a hiker!

290
00:17:02,388 --> 00:17:03,555
Yeah!

291
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:06,225
We believe it to be Ms. Tabatake.

292
00:17:08,494 --> 00:17:11,397
Ms. Motoka Tabatake, the guide.
Ms. Aya Saruwatari, a hiker…

293
00:17:11,463 --> 00:17:12,464
Aya?

294
00:17:13,098 --> 00:17:13,932
Is she safe?

295
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,871
Only Ms. Tabatake was found.

296
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:21,507
-Ms. Tabatake, you okay?
-Ten meters!

297
00:17:21,573 --> 00:17:23,575
-Ready for pickup!
-Pulling up!

298
00:17:23,642 --> 00:17:25,277
-Pulling up!
-Stand back.

299
00:17:25,344 --> 00:17:27,946
Going up! Stand back!

300
00:17:29,648 --> 00:17:31,950
She's unconscious.
We're sending her over there.

301
00:17:34,119 --> 00:17:37,289
Nono. They found your mom.

302
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:41,894
What about Ms. Saruwatari?

303
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:43,162
Only her belongings.

304
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:49,234
We found a hiking insurance
application form in a stream, east side.

305
00:17:50,269 --> 00:17:51,236
A stream…

306
00:17:51,770 --> 00:17:53,172
So she came down the mountain?

307
00:17:53,238 --> 00:17:55,541
Maybe. We're searching
the surrounding area carefully.

308
00:17:55,607 --> 00:17:56,442
Ogoma!

309
00:17:57,109 --> 00:17:58,210
They found a hiker!

310
00:17:58,777 --> 00:18:00,479
I just got back from a house call.

311
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:08,320
Thank goodness.

312
00:18:09,221 --> 00:18:11,924
She's coming to this hospital now.
You'll see her soon.

313
00:18:11,990 --> 00:18:13,325
Isn't that great, Nono?

314
00:18:13,392 --> 00:18:16,628
Thank goodness, huh.

315
00:18:16,695 --> 00:18:18,464
One of the missing?

316
00:18:20,399 --> 00:18:23,001
Nono's mom is a mountain guide.

317
00:18:23,068 --> 00:18:25,637
-Oh, Ms. Tabatake?
-Yes!

318
00:18:25,704 --> 00:18:28,340
-I'm glad she was found.
-Right?

319
00:18:28,407 --> 00:18:30,509
Nono has no father.

320
00:18:30,576 --> 00:18:34,079
If her mom disappeared too,
I would be so worried.

321
00:18:34,146 --> 00:18:37,216
What is she being treated for?

322
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:40,185
I don't know.
Something with her immune system.

323
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:41,920
-Thank you.
-No problem.

324
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:52,297
VISITOR PASS

325
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:56,335
44 HOURS LEFT

326
00:18:57,503 --> 00:18:59,905
Search operations for all teams
will end at sunset.

327
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:02,508
Let's do our best to find
the other four missing!

328
00:19:02,574 --> 00:19:04,243
If you can hear us, please answer!

329
00:19:04,309 --> 00:19:05,477
Ogoma.

330
00:19:07,913 --> 00:19:12,117
Tomorrow, we'll have more
local rescue workers joining us

331
00:19:12,184 --> 00:19:13,919
to expand the search area.

332
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,455
28 hours have already passed.

333
00:19:16,522 --> 00:19:18,423
Keep up the good work tomorrow!

334
00:19:27,966 --> 00:19:29,234
Hello.

335
00:19:29,301 --> 00:19:30,402
Hello.

336
00:19:41,246 --> 00:19:42,080
Hup.

337
00:19:44,416 --> 00:19:46,485
Your mom's body is exhausted.

338
00:19:46,552 --> 00:19:48,053
She's resting now.

339
00:19:49,054 --> 00:19:51,790
It will take time for her to wake up.
Let's wait.

340
00:19:53,258 --> 00:19:54,927
Will she really wake up?

341
00:19:56,295 --> 00:19:57,362
It's okay.

342
00:19:58,363 --> 00:19:59,831
Your mom is strong.

343
00:20:11,677 --> 00:20:13,645
-Good job.
-Good work today!

344
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:15,781
Ms. Tabatake isn't doing well.

345
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:20,252
She has severe hypothermia
and blood loss, and is in the ICU.

346
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:22,020
I hope she wakes up.

347
00:20:22,087 --> 00:20:22,988
Right?

348
00:20:23,055 --> 00:20:24,690
Four more people.

349
00:20:25,357 --> 00:20:28,727
Ms. Saruwatari, the Monden couple,
and Mr. Uematsu.

350
00:20:28,794 --> 00:20:31,263
The families waiting for them
have it rough too.

351
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:33,031
Ms. Saruwatari…

352
00:20:33,098 --> 00:20:35,133
I might know her.

353
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,201
Huh?

354
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:38,437
It could be a person with the same name.
I'm not sure.

355
00:20:38,503 --> 00:20:41,073
I hope they hold out.

356
00:20:41,139 --> 00:20:43,141
-Chief.
-Huh?

357
00:20:43,208 --> 00:20:45,210
Can we really ignore
that insurance investigator?

358
00:20:45,277 --> 00:20:46,111
Tsukasa Nao.

359
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:47,479
Nao, Zennichi Insurance Research.

360
00:20:47,546 --> 00:20:50,282
That guy,
he was at the response office too.

361
00:20:50,349 --> 00:20:53,652
He was asking everyone questions,
as though he was part of the operation.

362
00:20:54,152 --> 00:20:55,420
What is he investigating?

363
00:20:56,021 --> 00:20:57,556
Teruyuki Nikaido.

364
00:20:57,623 --> 00:21:00,525
When an insured person gets hurt or dies,

365
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:02,361
the insurance company pays money, right?

366
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:06,231
-Yeah.
-They don't always pay the full amount.

367
00:21:06,298 --> 00:21:09,468
They check if there
is anything suspicious in the claim.

368
00:21:09,534 --> 00:21:10,936
Is he an insurance company employee?

369
00:21:11,003 --> 00:21:14,506
No. He works for a company
that only does investigations.

370
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,342
I heard he's very persistent.

371
00:21:17,409 --> 00:21:19,444
He's more insensitive than persistent.

372
00:21:20,078 --> 00:21:23,248
Remember the Hakodate
fake family suicide case?

373
00:21:23,315 --> 00:21:25,417
The husband's mistress was the culprit.

374
00:21:25,484 --> 00:21:27,486
I wasn't born back then.

375
00:21:27,552 --> 00:21:30,088
You were born and at the police academy.

376
00:21:31,089 --> 00:21:32,924
Nao investigated the insurance claim.

377
00:21:32,991 --> 00:21:36,995
He reported it as a murder to the police
which led to it becoming a case.

378
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:40,565
Why are we police losing
to an insurance investigator?

379
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:42,301
Don't lose, police!

380
00:21:42,367 --> 00:21:45,804
The police have to solve case after case.

381
00:21:46,405 --> 00:21:49,241
Well, not like lots of cases
happen around here.

382
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:52,244
Well, yeah, but…

383
00:21:52,878 --> 00:21:55,714
Insurance investigators
spend lots of time on one case.

384
00:21:55,781 --> 00:21:58,050
They probably have a bigger budget too.

385
00:21:58,116 --> 00:22:01,653
He might be amazing. But I don't like him.

386
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:04,089
He does help us out sometimes.

387
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:06,525
So cooperate with him as much as you can.

388
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:09,194
-Ogoma.
-Yes?

389
00:22:09,261 --> 00:22:10,962
-You want a promotion, right?
-I do.

390
00:22:11,029 --> 00:22:13,598
If you stay close to him,
he might give you info.

391
00:22:13,665 --> 00:22:15,734
I prioritize rescuing people.

392
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:20,639
Tomorrow, the fire brigade
and the mountain club will join us.

393
00:22:22,107 --> 00:22:24,343
Let me go into the mountain too.

394
00:22:24,409 --> 00:22:26,178
Leave it to people who know the mountain.

395
00:22:26,244 --> 00:22:29,181
I've been on that mountain
more than those outsiders have.

396
00:22:29,247 --> 00:22:30,982
We don't have enough people.

397
00:22:31,049 --> 00:22:32,584
So let me help out.

398
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,321
I'll be back by three.

399
00:22:58,343 --> 00:23:00,112
Hey. Detective?

400
00:23:01,179 --> 00:23:03,448
How did you know where I live?

401
00:23:03,515 --> 00:23:04,683
Who told you?

402
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:07,085
Huh? No.

403
00:23:07,619 --> 00:23:10,322
-My place is there.
-Where?

404
00:23:11,156 --> 00:23:12,457
Right there.

405
00:23:13,258 --> 00:23:14,292
What?!

406
00:23:14,359 --> 00:23:15,527
I'm closing the door.

407
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:18,764
Okay.

408
00:23:19,664 --> 00:23:20,799
Nobody lives there!

409
00:23:20,866 --> 00:23:24,436
I rented that empty room
for this business trip.

410
00:23:24,503 --> 00:23:27,472
Rescue workers filled up
all the other inns. Bye.

411
00:23:29,174 --> 00:23:31,777
Oh, by the way. Mr. Tanaka…

412
00:23:31,843 --> 00:23:33,111
That's not my name.

413
00:23:33,178 --> 00:23:34,846
I forgot your name.

414
00:23:34,913 --> 00:23:36,648
I haven't told you my name.

415
00:23:36,715 --> 00:23:39,184
I'm Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research.

416
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:41,787
I'm Ogoma from the Shikara Police Station.

417
00:23:41,853 --> 00:23:43,088
-Mr. Ogoma.
-Yes.

418
00:23:43,155 --> 00:23:44,456
Mr. Ogoma.

419
00:23:44,523 --> 00:23:45,490
Yes, that's me.

420
00:23:45,557 --> 00:23:47,726
Did you talk to Ms. Nikaido after that?

421
00:23:48,627 --> 00:23:50,395
Did you find out anything else?

422
00:23:50,462 --> 00:23:53,965
Ms. Nikaido fainted from anemia.
Who do you think caused that?

423
00:23:55,867 --> 00:23:56,735
Who could it be?

424
00:23:56,802 --> 00:23:59,137
I know it's your job,
but don't get in the way of the police.

425
00:23:59,204 --> 00:24:00,138
Of course.

426
00:24:01,973 --> 00:24:04,376
You plan to go into the mountain,
don't you?

427
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:05,444
Do I?

428
00:24:05,510 --> 00:24:08,246
Please don't go in on your own.
You could go missing.

429
00:24:09,314 --> 00:24:12,284
I'll join as part of the mountain club.
I'm good with mountains.

430
00:24:12,350 --> 00:24:14,152
Are you making that up?

431
00:24:15,454 --> 00:24:17,722
I was in the mountaineering club
in college.

432
00:24:18,256 --> 00:24:21,793
I've also handled
many mountain accident insurance cases.

433
00:24:25,096 --> 00:24:26,298
Is this real?

434
00:24:27,732 --> 00:24:28,633
Huh?

435
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:30,101
You doubt me?

436
00:24:31,603 --> 00:24:33,505
You've looked suspicious
since you got here.

437
00:24:33,572 --> 00:24:35,440
That's good!

438
00:24:36,074 --> 00:24:37,742
Doubt everything.

439
00:24:38,510 --> 00:24:39,177
Huh?

440
00:24:40,011 --> 00:24:43,181
Once you have doubted everything,
what remains…

441
00:24:43,248 --> 00:24:44,716
is the truth.

442
00:24:48,787 --> 00:24:50,055
The truth about what?

443
00:24:50,889 --> 00:24:51,823
Good night.

444
00:25:02,367 --> 00:25:04,269
Day two of the search.
Thank you, everyone.

445
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:05,370
Let's do our best!

446
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:08,006
Thank you to the fire brigade
and the mountain club too.

447
00:25:08,607 --> 00:25:10,709
Four missing people remain!

448
00:25:10,775 --> 00:25:12,677
Let's find them today, no matter what.

449
00:25:12,744 --> 00:25:13,979
Yes!

450
00:25:15,247 --> 00:25:17,415
Let's give it our all!

451
00:25:17,482 --> 00:25:18,917
Let's set off.

452
00:25:21,253 --> 00:25:22,754
Shall we go?

453
00:25:22,821 --> 00:25:25,557
-Come on.
-Let's do this.

454
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:29,361
-Is anyone there?
-Can you hear me?

455
00:25:34,499 --> 00:25:36,201
Mr. Monden!

456
00:25:38,670 --> 00:25:40,205
Is anyone there?

457
00:25:40,805 --> 00:25:42,240
Can you hear me?

458
00:25:43,975 --> 00:25:45,911
Have you ever climbed this mountain?

459
00:25:45,977 --> 00:25:47,045
Of course.

460
00:25:47,112 --> 00:25:50,315
I usually look for people
who get stuck picking wild vegetables.

461
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:52,484
A police detective has to do that?

462
00:25:52,551 --> 00:25:55,153
They make me do everything.
I'm the lowest rank.

463
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:57,722
-How many years have you been a detective?
-That doesn't matter.

464
00:25:57,789 --> 00:26:00,158
I guess six, seven years?

465
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:04,496
In Sapporo or Asahikawa,
you would get big cases by now.

466
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:05,664
Can you hear me?

467
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:08,166
I won't stay at the bottom forever.

468
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:10,101
Search team six to base.

469
00:26:10,168 --> 00:26:12,437
We'll go off-course to the southeast.

470
00:26:12,504 --> 00:26:13,872
Wait!

471
00:26:13,939 --> 00:26:16,875
Ms. Saruwatari's belongings
were found at the stream, right?

472
00:26:16,942 --> 00:26:19,778
If she lost her way,
Ms. Saruwatari would climb to the ridge.

473
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:22,213
Does she know mountains well?

474
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:26,251
Hey, you are the one who told me
this mountain was risky!

475
00:26:30,021 --> 00:26:31,890
You look lame!

476
00:26:32,457 --> 00:26:33,959
Where are you having lunch?

477
00:26:37,896 --> 00:26:39,097
Hey, stop it!

478
00:26:39,164 --> 00:26:42,000
-Miss!
-Join us!

479
00:26:42,067 --> 00:26:44,302
Sure, once I'm done with this.

480
00:26:44,369 --> 00:26:46,071
Ogoma, everyone has to go!

481
00:26:46,137 --> 00:26:47,639
Let's be in the same group.

482
00:26:47,706 --> 00:26:48,673
Sure.

483
00:26:51,843 --> 00:26:53,345
I'm not going.

484
00:26:53,912 --> 00:26:55,447
Let's invite Imai too.

485
00:26:55,513 --> 00:26:57,382
Sounds good.

486
00:27:04,522 --> 00:27:05,357
Ogoma.

487
00:27:07,692 --> 00:27:08,760
Ogoma.

488
00:27:10,128 --> 00:27:11,096
Good morning.

489
00:27:12,163 --> 00:27:14,933
Ogoma. Let's go to class.

490
00:27:19,838 --> 00:27:21,039
Ogoma.

491
00:27:21,106 --> 00:27:23,141
What are you doing? Come back.

492
00:27:23,675 --> 00:27:25,543
We'll take a break
once we reach that peak.

493
00:27:25,610 --> 00:27:27,545
-Ogoma.
-Yes!

494
00:27:27,612 --> 00:27:28,613
Over here.

495
00:27:39,691 --> 00:27:41,059
Is this the right way?

496
00:27:41,126 --> 00:27:44,029
Let me check.
This is search team six to base.

497
00:27:44,095 --> 00:27:47,732
-We went off course…
-Where is he going?

498
00:27:49,367 --> 00:27:51,302
-Can you hear me?
-Ogoma.

499
00:27:51,369 --> 00:27:52,804
You have to stop soon.

500
00:27:54,539 --> 00:27:56,041
Got to find them by today.

501
00:27:56,107 --> 00:27:57,442
We'll run into bears here.

502
00:27:58,043 --> 00:27:59,544
If a bear shows up, I'll fight it.

503
00:27:59,611 --> 00:28:01,246
A brown bear? Are you serious?

504
00:28:01,312 --> 00:28:02,147
Yes.

505
00:28:02,714 --> 00:28:06,317
-Let's go back. This old man is tired.
-It will be cold tonight.

506
00:28:06,384 --> 00:28:07,919
We must find them by today…

507
00:28:07,986 --> 00:28:08,853
Please answer…

508
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:11,589
-Is anyone there? Can you hear me?
-The critical 72 hours?

509
00:28:12,257 --> 00:28:13,124
Yeah.

510
00:28:13,892 --> 00:28:16,161
Is anyone there? Can you hear me?

511
00:28:16,227 --> 00:28:17,696
Let's take a break and think…

512
00:28:17,762 --> 00:28:18,663
Please answer!

513
00:28:18,730 --> 00:28:19,597
Can you hear me?

514
00:28:19,664 --> 00:28:21,800
-Ogoma.
-Answer me!

515
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:22,834
Hey!

516
00:28:25,003 --> 00:28:26,905
Break! Break time!

517
00:28:26,971 --> 00:28:30,809
Break time.

518
00:28:35,246 --> 00:28:36,748
Come on.

519
00:28:37,315 --> 00:28:38,450
You too, Ogoma.

520
00:28:38,516 --> 00:28:39,384
Here.

521
00:28:39,951 --> 00:28:40,785
Refuel.

522
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,160
Thanks.

523
00:28:55,633 --> 00:28:59,137
You came to investigate
Mr. Nikaido's life insurance, right?

524
00:28:59,971 --> 00:29:01,005
Yeah.

525
00:29:01,806 --> 00:29:05,210
I can't write my report
without knowing what happened.

526
00:29:07,178 --> 00:29:09,581
You had a reason
to press his wife so hard.

527
00:29:13,184 --> 00:29:15,653
Well, yeah. I did things by the book.

528
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:17,989
There is no "book" here.
You suspected her.

529
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:21,326
Can't you tell me?

530
00:29:27,732 --> 00:29:29,067
Harune…

531
00:29:30,168 --> 00:29:36,074
filed a life insurance claim
right after her husband's body was found.

532
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:40,044
Before the death certificate
was even issued.

533
00:29:40,578 --> 00:29:42,046
It's not issued yet, right?

534
00:29:42,714 --> 00:29:43,581
Yeah.

535
00:29:43,648 --> 00:29:45,316
We're waiting for the autopsy.

536
00:29:45,850 --> 00:29:46,951
How much is the insurance?

537
00:29:47,018 --> 00:29:48,286
150 million yen.

538
00:29:48,353 --> 00:29:50,321
It was increased two months ago.

539
00:29:51,923 --> 00:29:53,424
She has a reason to want it fast.

540
00:29:53,491 --> 00:29:56,227
She runs a restaurant
and has many employees.

541
00:29:56,294 --> 00:29:59,130
Still, isn't that too fast?

542
00:29:59,898 --> 00:30:04,135
Usually, people don't view a dead body
as a cash payout right away.

543
00:30:04,202 --> 00:30:06,638
So I want to know what happened.

544
00:30:09,874 --> 00:30:13,545
I want to hear from Mr. Nikaido's
companions about why he died.

545
00:30:13,611 --> 00:30:14,546
You do too, right?

546
00:30:18,883 --> 00:30:19,818
Huh?

547
00:30:19,884 --> 00:30:21,319
Search team to base.

548
00:30:21,386 --> 00:30:24,823
We found an aluminum blanket
that could have belonged to them!

549
00:30:48,379 --> 00:30:49,514
He's so fast.

550
00:31:05,630 --> 00:31:07,665
Hey! I can't keep up!

551
00:31:48,373 --> 00:31:50,441
How did he even find her here…

552
00:31:56,881 --> 00:31:59,417
Ms. Saruwatari. Open your eyes!

553
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:00,885
Ms. Saruwatari.

554
00:32:03,521 --> 00:32:04,455
Ms. Saruwatari.

555
00:32:05,523 --> 00:32:06,724
Ms. Aya!

556
00:32:12,063 --> 00:32:14,299
Ms. Aya. Are you okay?

557
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:16,401
Sorry…

558
00:32:16,467 --> 00:32:18,469
Don't move her!

559
00:32:18,536 --> 00:32:20,371
Ms. Saruwatari, are you okay?

560
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:21,773
-Sorry…
-Are you okay?

561
00:32:21,839 --> 00:32:24,709
-Ogoma. Is she wet?
-Yes.

562
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:27,278
Take off her jacket.
Her body temperature is dropping.

563
00:32:27,879 --> 00:32:28,713
Okay.

564
00:32:29,247 --> 00:32:31,649
Ms. Aya. I'll take your jacket off.

565
00:32:31,716 --> 00:32:32,617
Be gentle.

566
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:35,119
Are you okay? I'm taking it off.

567
00:32:35,186 --> 00:32:36,688
Wait a moment.

568
00:32:36,754 --> 00:32:39,023
Her arm may be broken.

569
00:32:39,824 --> 00:32:41,025
Don't force it.

570
00:32:41,993 --> 00:32:42,994
Are you okay?

571
00:32:43,061 --> 00:32:44,128
Here.

572
00:32:45,029 --> 00:32:46,731
-Put it under her arm.
-Thank you.

573
00:32:47,332 --> 00:32:49,367
-Can I lift your arm a bit?
-Be gentle.

574
00:32:52,036 --> 00:32:54,038
Search team six to base.

575
00:32:54,105 --> 00:32:56,107
We found Ms. Aya Saruwatari.

576
00:32:56,741 --> 00:32:58,810
East side of the mountain.

577
00:32:59,877 --> 00:33:02,013
540 meters high.

578
00:33:02,613 --> 00:33:04,115
Please send rescue.

579
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:06,317
-So cool.
-Are you okay?

580
00:33:06,384 --> 00:33:08,686
-Give me another heat pack.
-Okay, sure.

581
00:33:09,687 --> 00:33:13,391
ORIENT DINER

582
00:33:18,596 --> 00:33:20,264
Ms. Harune,
what happened to the president?

583
00:33:20,331 --> 00:33:22,200
He died. He is dead.

584
00:33:25,603 --> 00:33:26,471
Harune!

585
00:33:26,537 --> 00:33:28,773
If he's dead, what happens to this place?

586
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:30,141
I'll contact you when I find out.

587
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:31,476
The president is dead?

588
00:33:31,542 --> 00:33:32,610
Why?

589
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:35,013
I don't know. I want to ask her too.

590
00:33:35,079 --> 00:33:36,914
What are we supposed to do now?

591
00:33:36,981 --> 00:33:39,150
Why isn't she telling us anything?

592
00:33:39,217 --> 00:33:40,818
Hey, explain!

593
00:33:40,885 --> 00:33:43,021
I told you, I'll contact when I find out.

594
00:33:43,087 --> 00:33:44,889
Really? What do we do now?

595
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:49,794
-What should we do?
-Can't you see I'm busy?

596
00:34:05,176 --> 00:34:06,444
Ms. Saruwatari.

597
00:34:06,944 --> 00:34:08,746
Are you in pain?

598
00:34:09,614 --> 00:34:10,948
-Yes.
-Any other issues…

599
00:34:11,015 --> 00:34:12,884
She's your teacher? From when?

600
00:34:13,584 --> 00:34:15,119
Back in middle school.

601
00:34:15,853 --> 00:34:16,921
Well…

602
00:34:16,988 --> 00:34:19,057
She was just a trainee teacher.

603
00:34:19,123 --> 00:34:20,591
And you remember her name?

604
00:34:21,659 --> 00:34:23,761
-Yeah.
-Amazing.

605
00:34:25,263 --> 00:34:27,465
You did well to find her there.

606
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:33,137
At my school, the whole school
climbed that mountain for class.

607
00:34:33,204 --> 00:34:35,406
We couldn't graduate if we skipped.

608
00:34:35,473 --> 00:34:37,141
So you actually climbed it.

609
00:34:38,376 --> 00:34:42,513
The trail we used then
is damaged now and not used anymore.

610
00:34:43,514 --> 00:34:45,483
I figured she might not know that,

611
00:34:45,550 --> 00:34:49,187
and might try to use the old trail
and go down the ridge.

612
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:52,990
Oh, you still remember
your middle school days so well.

613
00:34:53,057 --> 00:34:55,660
I only remember studying.

614
00:34:56,928 --> 00:34:59,097
I don't want to remember it much.

615
00:34:59,163 --> 00:34:59,997
Why?

616
00:35:01,232 --> 00:35:03,134
One memory

617
00:35:03,935 --> 00:35:06,404
makes everything come back,
and it's annoying.

618
00:35:07,705 --> 00:35:09,841
My mind gets messed up.

619
00:35:11,976 --> 00:35:13,177
Detective.

620
00:35:13,244 --> 00:35:14,612
Yes.

621
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:19,183
Here.

622
00:35:20,184 --> 00:35:22,453
I won't get in your way.

623
00:35:23,387 --> 00:35:24,422
Follow me.

624
00:35:27,458 --> 00:35:28,893
-Thank you very much.
-Okay.

625
00:35:30,661 --> 00:35:31,996
See you later.

626
00:35:40,571 --> 00:35:43,374
A police officer wants to talk to you.

627
00:35:43,441 --> 00:35:45,710
This is the detective who found you.

628
00:35:47,712 --> 00:35:48,713
20 HOURS LEFT

629
00:35:48,779 --> 00:35:49,914
Please come in.

630
00:35:51,749 --> 00:35:55,086
Her left arm is broken.
She's on painkillers.

631
00:35:55,786 --> 00:35:57,155
Please keep it short.

632
00:35:57,221 --> 00:35:58,156
Yes.

633
00:36:01,325 --> 00:36:03,227
Excuse me. I'm from the Shikara--

634
00:36:03,294 --> 00:36:04,562
I'm sorry

635
00:36:05,930 --> 00:36:07,398
for the trouble.

636
00:36:13,638 --> 00:36:16,874
Is your pain a little better now?

637
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:18,676
Yes.

638
00:36:19,977 --> 00:36:24,115
The doctor says once I recover a bit,
I'll have surgery.

639
00:36:24,649 --> 00:36:25,483
Okay.

640
00:36:25,550 --> 00:36:27,018
I heard Ms. Tabatake

641
00:36:27,985 --> 00:36:30,288
is in the ICU.

642
00:36:31,389 --> 00:36:32,823
What about Mr. Nikaido?

643
00:36:33,991 --> 00:36:36,460
We found him. But unfortunately…

644
00:36:40,898 --> 00:36:43,568
The others haven't been found yet.

645
00:36:45,636 --> 00:36:47,405
Were you all friends?

646
00:36:48,539 --> 00:36:49,507
No.

647
00:36:50,675 --> 00:36:52,276
We had just met.

648
00:36:52,343 --> 00:36:56,547
Can you tell me what happened?

649
00:37:00,885 --> 00:37:02,653
Did you take any photos?

650
00:37:08,726 --> 00:37:10,228
Do you remember their names?

651
00:37:11,762 --> 00:37:13,197
Ms. Tabatake.

652
00:37:13,264 --> 00:37:14,232
Yes.

653
00:37:15,032 --> 00:37:16,033
Mr. Monden.

654
00:37:16,100 --> 00:37:18,369
-Are you tired? You okay?
-I'm fine.

655
00:37:18,436 --> 00:37:19,737
His wife, Misaki.

656
00:37:19,804 --> 00:37:20,805
It's getting cold.

657
00:37:20,871 --> 00:37:22,273
Mr. Uematsu.

658
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:26,811
600 yen for a rice ball is too expensive!

659
00:37:27,511 --> 00:37:28,946
And water too.

660
00:37:29,013 --> 00:37:30,948
-That will be 200 yen.
-What?!

661
00:37:37,888 --> 00:37:39,090
Mr. Nikaido.

662
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:42,727
Excuse me.

663
00:37:44,428 --> 00:37:47,765
May I send some of these photos
to the response office?

664
00:37:47,832 --> 00:37:50,468
The search is still ongoing.

665
00:37:51,469 --> 00:37:52,470
Yes, please.

666
00:37:53,638 --> 00:37:55,573
Thank you for your help.

667
00:37:58,776 --> 00:38:01,245
Looks like it was nice weather
on the way up.

668
00:38:03,381 --> 00:38:04,382
Yes.

669
00:38:06,884 --> 00:38:10,554
When we started going down,
lightning started coming down.

670
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:15,359
The lightning is getting closer.

671
00:38:15,426 --> 00:38:17,161
Let's find a safe place to wait this out.

672
00:38:19,563 --> 00:38:23,567
Ms. Tabatake said,
"Let's rest until the storm passes."

673
00:38:26,704 --> 00:38:28,439
It's cold.

674
00:38:28,506 --> 00:38:29,974
I have a heat pack.

675
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:32,109
Mr. Nikaido looks lightly dressed.

676
00:38:32,176 --> 00:38:34,945
Mr. Nikaido. Please use this.

677
00:38:35,012 --> 00:38:36,213
I don't need it.

678
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,349
Then it started to rain.

679
00:38:38,416 --> 00:38:42,219
He looked cold, and his face was pale.

680
00:38:42,286 --> 00:38:44,288
How were the others?

681
00:38:45,056 --> 00:38:46,891
Did they seem used to mountains?

682
00:38:49,226 --> 00:38:52,096
They seemed used to it.

683
00:38:55,633 --> 00:38:59,570
Even with experience,
you still decided to hire a guide?

684
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:07,011
Ms. Tabatake
knows mountain plants very well.

685
00:39:08,312 --> 00:39:10,981
I wanted to see
the flowers of this season,

686
00:39:11,048 --> 00:39:12,416
so I joined.

687
00:39:16,053 --> 00:39:17,722
So you like flowers.

688
00:39:19,557 --> 00:39:24,061
I started hiking
because I was interested in plants.

689
00:39:28,499 --> 00:39:29,433
But…

690
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:34,772
That was the scariest thing

691
00:39:36,574 --> 00:39:38,075
that ever happened to me.

692
00:39:41,779 --> 00:39:44,448
Mr. Monden! Misaki!

693
00:39:45,182 --> 00:39:47,985
Mr. Uematsu! Are you hurt?

694
00:39:48,652 --> 00:39:50,154
I'm okay!

695
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:51,455
I'm okay!

696
00:39:51,522 --> 00:39:52,490
Calm down!

697
00:39:53,190 --> 00:39:55,693
Stay calm and don't move!

698
00:39:56,260 --> 00:39:57,361
Yes!

699
00:39:57,428 --> 00:40:01,265
We'll wait here until the storm stops.

700
00:40:01,332 --> 00:40:03,801
-Are you okay?
-I'm going home.

701
00:40:03,868 --> 00:40:05,069
Don't move!

702
00:40:05,636 --> 00:40:07,371
I'm cold. A bath…

703
00:40:07,905 --> 00:40:09,974
-Mr. Nikaido!
-I want to take a bath…

704
00:40:10,608 --> 00:40:13,210
-Mr. Nikaido!
-Do you understand the situation?

705
00:40:13,277 --> 00:40:14,712
You could die!

706
00:40:14,779 --> 00:40:16,947
Mr. Nikaido, it's dangerous!

707
00:40:17,014 --> 00:40:18,783
Are you all right?

708
00:40:21,719 --> 00:40:23,120
I'll go bring him back.

709
00:40:23,187 --> 00:40:24,655
No, I will.

710
00:40:25,389 --> 00:40:27,758
Everyone, please don't move for a while.

711
00:40:28,926 --> 00:40:29,960
A heat pack.

712
00:40:30,694 --> 00:40:31,996
Thank you.

713
00:40:33,631 --> 00:40:36,133
After we couldn't hear
the thunder anymore,

714
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:39,203
neither Mr. Nikaido nor Ms. Tabatake

715
00:40:40,171 --> 00:40:41,672
came back.

716
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:46,577
What time was it?

717
00:40:48,078 --> 00:40:51,415
Around 3:00 p.m.

718
00:40:52,383 --> 00:40:54,485
It was getting cold in the mountains.

719
00:40:56,620 --> 00:41:01,058
The way back to the trail
was blocked by fallen trees.

720
00:41:01,125 --> 00:41:02,159
You okay?

721
00:41:02,226 --> 00:41:06,363
I didn't know how to lead them down.

722
00:41:07,798 --> 00:41:08,833
I…

723
00:41:08,899 --> 00:41:11,068
will go down and call for help.

724
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:12,937
No, don't push yourself!

725
00:41:13,003 --> 00:41:16,440
As soon as I get a phone signal,
I'll call for rescue.

726
00:41:16,507 --> 00:41:17,741
Please wait here.

727
00:41:17,808 --> 00:41:18,676
Ms. Saruwatari!

728
00:41:18,742 --> 00:41:20,110
Will she be okay?

729
00:41:20,177 --> 00:41:21,512
While going down,

730
00:41:22,279 --> 00:41:24,448
I thought I heard a scream.

731
00:41:25,115 --> 00:41:25,983
So…

732
00:41:26,817 --> 00:41:28,385
I went toward the stream.

733
00:41:32,256 --> 00:41:33,324
Ms. Tabatake!

734
00:41:33,991 --> 00:41:35,426
Where are you?

735
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:37,361
Please answer me.

736
00:41:38,429 --> 00:41:40,064
Mr. Nikaido!

737
00:41:41,599 --> 00:41:43,968
I made the wrong choice.

738
00:41:45,002 --> 00:41:48,506
I should have gone straight down
and called for help.

739
00:41:50,107 --> 00:41:53,944
No one can think clearly
in a situation like that.

740
00:41:54,812 --> 00:41:58,883
It's my fault we were late going down.

741
00:42:00,284 --> 00:42:01,886
I wanted to see flowers,

742
00:42:02,987 --> 00:42:04,855
so I stopped everyone many times.

743
00:42:05,456 --> 00:42:11,295
The others didn't care
about flowers at all.

744
00:42:19,336 --> 00:42:20,671
Ms. Saruwatari.

745
00:42:27,511 --> 00:42:30,981
I'm glad you're safe.

746
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:39,290
We will find the others.

747
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:50,501
If you remember anything
that could help the search,

748
00:42:51,335 --> 00:42:53,837
please contact me.

749
00:43:06,884 --> 00:43:07,885
Ogoma?

750
00:43:12,890 --> 00:43:14,091
Ogoma!

751
00:43:25,169 --> 00:43:27,338
Ogoma, are you okay?

752
00:43:28,072 --> 00:43:29,239
What's wrong?

753
00:43:30,708 --> 00:43:31,875
All right.

754
00:43:32,476 --> 00:43:33,811
It's okay.

755
00:43:35,079 --> 00:43:36,714
It's okay.

756
00:43:37,681 --> 00:43:39,617
I'm here.

757
00:43:40,184 --> 00:43:41,619
It's okay.

758
00:43:43,220 --> 00:43:44,321
Yes.

759
00:43:48,158 --> 00:43:49,360
You…

760
00:43:50,260 --> 00:43:52,062
You really are Ogoma.

761
00:43:53,063 --> 00:43:55,199
Hey, Ogoma, you okay?

762
00:43:55,833 --> 00:43:57,568
We have water. Want some?

763
00:43:57,635 --> 00:43:58,902
What's up, Ogoma?

764
00:43:58,969 --> 00:44:00,170
You okay?

765
00:44:00,237 --> 00:44:01,572
Want me to head down with you?

766
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,841
-Yeah.
-Thanks.

767
00:44:06,210 --> 00:44:07,344
Thank you.

768
00:44:09,013 --> 00:44:11,115
You saved my life.

769
00:44:13,584 --> 00:44:14,685
It's nothing.

770
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,454
Thank you.

771
00:44:20,557 --> 00:44:21,625
Yeah.

772
00:44:35,472 --> 00:44:37,207
-Thank you.
-Okay, take care.

773
00:44:38,709 --> 00:44:40,077
Take care.

774
00:44:40,144 --> 00:44:41,512
Take care.

775
00:44:43,914 --> 00:44:45,115
Thank you.

776
00:44:45,182 --> 00:44:46,050
Come in.

777
00:44:46,950 --> 00:44:48,519
Excuse me.

778
00:44:49,086 --> 00:44:50,287
I am…

779
00:44:50,988 --> 00:44:53,357
Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research.

780
00:44:54,324 --> 00:44:57,061
-I heard you wanted to discuss a disease?
-Yes.

781
00:44:57,695 --> 00:45:00,130
-Have a seat.
-Oh, excuse me.

782
00:45:00,664 --> 00:45:04,334
I would like to learn
about ECO deficiency,

783
00:45:04,401 --> 00:45:06,870
a designated incurable disease.

784
00:45:06,937 --> 00:45:10,507
-Sorry to bother you when you're busy.
-It's no problem.

785
00:45:10,574 --> 00:45:14,912
Dr. Yoshino,
you know this disease very well, right?

786
00:45:15,646 --> 00:45:17,848
I'm not a specialist.

787
00:45:18,382 --> 00:45:20,384
I see.

788
00:45:21,652 --> 00:45:25,255
I heard it's a very rare disease.

789
00:45:25,322 --> 00:45:26,490
Mommy!

790
00:45:27,324 --> 00:45:28,592
Mommy!

791
00:45:32,463 --> 00:45:33,764
Mommy!

792
00:45:34,965 --> 00:45:36,266
Mommy!

793
00:45:39,269 --> 00:45:40,471
SIX HOURS LEFT

794
00:45:41,505 --> 00:45:43,307
Please start a record.

795
00:45:43,373 --> 00:45:44,708
-Yes.
-Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.

796
00:45:44,775 --> 00:45:47,177
Date of birth is December 3, 1981.

797
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:49,213
-Excuse me.
-44 years old.

798
00:45:49,279 --> 00:45:52,382
He has no major
medical history or illness.

799
00:45:52,449 --> 00:45:56,787
We think a fall is the most likely cause,
but we will look at other possibilities.

800
00:45:56,854 --> 00:45:57,921
Let's begin.

801
00:45:57,988 --> 00:45:58,956
-Please do.
-Yes.

802
00:45:59,022 --> 00:46:00,324
Hello.

803
00:46:04,528 --> 00:46:05,662
What are the autopsy results?

804
00:46:05,729 --> 00:46:08,298
The cause of death is a brain injury
from a head wound.

805
00:46:08,365 --> 00:46:10,634
Maybe he lost consciousness and fell.

806
00:46:10,701 --> 00:46:13,003
That's what they told me.

807
00:46:13,070 --> 00:46:15,405
So it was just as it looked, right?

808
00:46:15,472 --> 00:46:17,274
-The blood test results are--
-Ogoma!

809
00:46:17,341 --> 00:46:18,542
-Come here.
-I'll call back.

810
00:46:18,609 --> 00:46:23,013
Zolpidem was found in Mr. Nikaido's blood.

811
00:46:23,080 --> 00:46:24,915
-Zolpidem?
-A sleeping pill.

812
00:46:25,816 --> 00:46:26,717
Huh?

813
00:46:26,784 --> 00:46:29,386
Mr. Nikaido doesn't take
any regular medicine, right?

814
00:46:30,487 --> 00:46:32,356
That's what his wife said.

815
00:46:33,357 --> 00:46:34,825
How much was in his blood?

816
00:46:34,892 --> 00:46:37,194
About 1.5 times the normal dose.

817
00:46:37,261 --> 00:46:42,332
After taking it, a person gets confused
and dizzy in 15 to 30 minutes.

818
00:46:42,399 --> 00:46:43,901
30 minutes.

819
00:46:44,668 --> 00:46:46,937
You wouldn't take that in the mountains.

820
00:46:47,004 --> 00:46:49,673
Did he take a sleeping pill while hiking?

821
00:46:50,707 --> 00:46:51,842
Think for yourself.

822
00:46:56,280 --> 00:46:57,981
Let's talk to his wife.

823
00:46:58,549 --> 00:47:00,751
Any possibility Mr. Nikaido was murdered?

824
00:47:00,818 --> 00:47:02,452
I think it had to be an accident.

825
00:47:03,487 --> 00:47:05,923
The tour guest we found yesterday

826
00:47:06,490 --> 00:47:09,126
said he went down the mountain alone,
on his own decision.

827
00:47:09,193 --> 00:47:11,428
Alone? No companion?

828
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:14,064
The guide went after him.

829
00:47:14,631 --> 00:47:18,635
But from where they were found,
they probably went separately.

830
00:47:20,904 --> 00:47:22,072
Look into it more.

831
00:47:22,139 --> 00:47:23,473
Why?

832
00:47:23,540 --> 00:47:27,077
I confirmed the hiking insurance
the tour guests had.

833
00:47:27,744 --> 00:47:30,314
All five had insurance.

834
00:47:32,449 --> 00:47:33,550
How much?

835
00:47:33,617 --> 00:47:34,751
Five million yen.

836
00:47:37,154 --> 00:47:40,390
Is Mr. Nikaido's hiking insurance
paid to his wife?

837
00:47:41,892 --> 00:47:43,760
You would think that, wouldn't you?

838
00:47:44,628 --> 00:47:45,562
What?

839
00:47:45,629 --> 00:47:47,965
If not her, then who is it paid to?

840
00:48:06,516 --> 00:48:07,784
Sleeping pills?

841
00:48:08,485 --> 00:48:11,555
It wasn't in your husband's
prescription history.

842
00:48:12,456 --> 00:48:15,158
Do you take sleeping pills?

843
00:48:15,225 --> 00:48:16,360
No.

844
00:48:17,094 --> 00:48:19,897
I can sleep fine without them.

845
00:48:22,766 --> 00:48:24,434
Isn't it strange?

846
00:48:25,469 --> 00:48:30,707
Why would he take a sleeping pill
in the middle of hiking?

847
00:48:31,541 --> 00:48:36,380
Could he have mistaken it
for a headache pill or cold medicine?

848
00:48:37,447 --> 00:48:39,182
He hates medicine.

849
00:48:39,883 --> 00:48:44,288
Even with a headache or a stomachache,
he takes nothing and just sleeps.

850
00:48:44,354 --> 00:48:45,689
So he never takes medicine himself.

851
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:46,723
No.

852
00:48:52,095 --> 00:48:54,564
When did you last talk to him?

853
00:48:55,432 --> 00:48:56,533
That would be…

854
00:48:58,568 --> 00:49:01,271
The morning he left.

855
00:49:01,338 --> 00:49:02,606
What did you talk about?

856
00:49:04,875 --> 00:49:06,310
He was in a bad mood.

857
00:49:09,046 --> 00:49:13,684
He said the bathroom drain was clogged,
and I should clean it before he got home.

858
00:49:14,618 --> 00:49:16,954
Is he always like that?

859
00:49:18,655 --> 00:49:19,723
Like what?

860
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:21,124
Bossy.

861
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:24,628
Yes.

862
00:49:27,230 --> 00:49:29,433
He has always been like that.

863
00:49:31,935 --> 00:49:33,103
That is…

864
00:49:35,005 --> 00:49:36,239
normal for us.

865
00:49:41,678 --> 00:49:46,016
Did Mr. Teruyuki
have anyone who hated him?

866
00:49:49,920 --> 00:49:51,121
I don't know.

867
00:49:52,656 --> 00:49:55,359
What is this? What do you want to know?

868
00:49:56,860 --> 00:50:00,630
Whether someone made him
take the sleeping pill or not.

869
00:50:04,234 --> 00:50:06,336
Don't ask me that!

870
00:50:07,237 --> 00:50:10,440
How would I know? Ask someone else.

871
00:50:16,380 --> 00:50:17,981
I feel sick.

872
00:50:18,582 --> 00:50:19,449
Huh?

873
00:50:20,884 --> 00:50:21,818
Harune…

874
00:50:21,885 --> 00:50:23,887
-Where is the restroom?
-Over here.

875
00:50:24,688 --> 00:50:28,258
-Move.
-Harune, we're not done talking.

876
00:50:28,325 --> 00:50:29,760
Harune!

877
00:50:31,828 --> 00:50:33,030
Waiting is part of the job.

878
00:50:33,096 --> 00:50:35,065
-Just leave me be!
-Yeah, but…

879
00:50:43,673 --> 00:50:46,610
-Yes.
-It's Nao. Thanks for the other day.

880
00:50:46,676 --> 00:50:48,278
How do you know my number?

881
00:50:48,345 --> 00:50:51,748
All five tour guests
took out hiking insurance.

882
00:50:51,815 --> 00:50:53,517
Thanks for the info.

883
00:50:54,618 --> 00:50:56,520
Who do you think
gets the money if they die?

884
00:50:56,586 --> 00:50:57,954
Their families, right?

885
00:50:58,021 --> 00:51:00,057
Usually, yes.

886
00:51:00,957 --> 00:51:02,259
I'm working right now.

887
00:51:02,325 --> 00:51:06,563
The beneficiary for Mr. Monden, his wife,
Mr. Uematsu, and Mr. Nikaido

888
00:51:07,397 --> 00:51:09,366
is Aya Saruwatari.

889
00:51:15,439 --> 00:51:16,873
OPERATING ROOM

890
00:51:16,940 --> 00:51:21,278
Five million yen each and four people.
That's twenty million yen.

891
00:51:21,344 --> 00:51:23,346
If all four die…

892
00:51:26,383 --> 00:51:30,387
Ms. Saruwatari gets twenty million yen.

893
00:51:34,724 --> 00:51:35,692
What?

894
00:51:37,194 --> 00:51:39,329
That has to be a mistake.

895
00:51:40,063 --> 00:51:41,832
Did you talk to Harune?

896
00:51:41,898 --> 00:51:44,434
She said she felt sick again.

897
00:51:44,501 --> 00:51:45,836
Maybe it's an act.

898
00:51:45,902 --> 00:51:46,903
Maybe.

899
00:51:46,970 --> 00:51:47,804
Ogoma.

900
00:51:47,871 --> 00:51:49,806
This isn't just a missing person case.

901
00:51:51,108 --> 00:51:53,076
It's a crime, not an accident.

902
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:56,746
At least, that's what I think.

903
00:52:01,918 --> 00:52:03,153
Mommy!

904
00:52:12,362 --> 00:52:15,632
You mean insurance murder?

905
00:52:22,072 --> 00:52:23,540
Am I a suspect now?

906
00:52:23,607 --> 00:52:27,043
Either Ms. Tabatake
or Ms. Aya is the accomplice.

907
00:52:27,110 --> 00:52:28,845
I may have been wrong.

908
00:52:28,912 --> 00:52:29,846
Ogoma!

909
00:52:29,913 --> 00:52:30,914
Please send backup.

910
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:31,948
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

911
00:52:31,948 --> 00:52:32,948

